 1296:    // ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 1297:    // These are functions that work on all nodes/sides of the element.
 1298:    // They use a standard, but not well known, way of accessing the fields of the nodes.
 1299:    //
 1300:    // An example of how to use these functions is:
 1301:    //   
 1302:    //    getNodalValues(L, &Node::compZCoord, zLAtNodes);
 1303:    // 
 1304:    // Where L is the level at which the field is to be interpolated. The field can be either
 1305:    // a double (depth), an array (u[nvrt]), or a function that depends on the level (Node::compZCoord(int k)). 
 1306:    // There are different versions of getNodalValues for each of these cases.
 1307: 
